### Smoke + end-to-end scenarios for the 3-service setup (auth/claim/penalty).
### IntelliJ HTTP Client syntax: `> {% client.global.set(...) %}` captures ids
### from responses; subsequent requests use `{{name_id}}`.
### All requests go through auth-service on :8080 (HTTP Basic auth).
### Run via "Run all in file" or top-to-bottom — later blocks depend on earlier ids.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

@adminEmail = admin@blps.local
@adminPass = adminpass
@landlordEmail = landlord@blps.local
@landlordPass = landpass
@tenantEmail = tenant@blps.local
@tenantPass = tenantpass

### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###  0. Bootstrap users (re-runs are idempotent — 409 means "already there")
### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 0.1 Register landlord
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{landlordEmail}}", "password": "{{landlordPass}}", "role": "LANDLORD" }

> {%
client.test("register landlord ok or already exists", () => {
  client.assert(response.status === 201 || response.status === 409, "got " + response.status);
});
%}

### 0.2 Register tenant
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{tenantEmail}}", "password": "{{tenantPass}}", "role": "TENANT" }

> {%
client.test("register tenant ok or already exists", () => {
  client.assert(response.status === 201 || response.status === 409, "got " + response.status);
});
%}

### 0.3 Admin must be seeded via SQL (sql/init_auth_service.sql).

### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###  1. Smoke — Basic auth + identity
### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1.1 Who am I (landlord)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}

> {%
client.global.set("landlord_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 1.2 Who am I (tenant)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Basic {{tenantEmail}} {{tenantPass}}

> {%
client.global.set("tenant_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 1.3 Who am I (admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

> {%
client.global.set("admin_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 1.4 List users (admin-only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###  2. Scenario A — Happy path: claim → assessment → penalty applied
### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 2.1 Landlord creates claim
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": {{tenant_id}},
  "title": "Broken sofa and stained carpet",
  "description": "Tenant left visible damage; landlord requests damage assessment.",
  "claimedAmount": 250.00,
  "currency": "USD"
}

> {%
client.global.set("claimA_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 2.2 Read created claim
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}

### 2.3 Admin starts intake
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA_id}}/intake-start
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 2.4 Admin asks for additional info
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA_id}}/intake-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestAdditionalInfo": true, "note": "Please attach photos and serial numbers." }

### 2.5 Landlord provides additional info
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA_id}}/additional-info
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Attached photos and the sofa serial number; carpet visible in room overview." }

### 2.6 Admin records the assessment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA_id}}/assessment
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "penaltyGrounds": true, "assessmentAmount": 175.00, "assessmentNotes": "Damage confirmed; reduced to fair value." }

### 2.7 Tenant disagrees
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA_id}}/tenant-response
Authorization: Basic {{tenantEmail}} {{tenantPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "I disagree with the assessed amount." }

### 2.8 Support approves penalty application
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA_id}}/support-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applyPenalty": true,
  "penaltyAmount": 175.00,
  "penaltyCurrency": "USD",
  "simulateFailure": false,
  "resolutionNote": "Proceed with penalty application."
}

### 2.9 Poll claim until PENALTY_APPLIED (Outbox+Kafka are async — re-run a few times)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}

### 2.10 Claim status history
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA_id}}/history
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 2.11 Penalty for this claim (penalty-service via proxy)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/penalties/claim/{{claimA_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###  3. Scenario B — Penalty failure → manual retry
### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###  Moved to 31-lab3-penalty-failure-recovery.http: that flow depends on
###  Outbox→Kafka→penalty-service lag (~1-2s), which "Run all in file" can't
###  wait on. Run that file step-by-step instead.
### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###  4. Scenario C — User deactivation
### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 4.1 Create a throwaway tenant
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "deactivateme@blps.local", "password": "tmppass1", "role": "TENANT" }

> {%
if (response.status === 201 && response.body && response.body.id) {
  client.global.set("deactUser_id", response.body.id);
}
%}

### 4.2 If 409 above, look the user up (admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

> {%
if (Array.isArray(response.body)) {
  const u = response.body.find(x => x.email === "deactivateme@blps.local");
  if (u) client.global.set("deactUser_id", u.id);
}
%}

### 4.3 Admin deactivates them
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{deactUser_id}}/deactivate
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 4.4 Verify enabled=false
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{deactUser_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###  5. Scenario D — Claim closed without penalty
### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 5.1 Create + intake + assessment with no penalty grounds
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": {{tenant_id}},
  "title": "No-damage claim",
  "description": "Tenant returned unit in good condition.",
  "claimedAmount": 50.00,
  "currency": "USD"
}

> {%
client.global.set("claimD_id", response.body.id);
%}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimD_id}}/intake-start
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimD_id}}/intake-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestAdditionalInfo": false, "note": "" }

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimD_id}}/assessment
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "penaltyGrounds": false, "assessmentAmount": 0, "assessmentNotes": "No damage observed." }

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimD_id}}/tenant-response
Authorization: Basic {{tenantEmail}} {{tenantPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Thanks, all good." }

### 5.2 Support closes without penalty
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimD_id}}/support-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applyPenalty": false,
  "penaltyAmount": 0,
  "penaltyCurrency": "USD",
  "simulateFailure": false,
  "resolutionNote": "Closed without penalty."
}

### 5.3 Verify CLOSED_NO_PENALTY
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimD_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}

### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###  6. Messages on a claim
### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 6.1 Landlord adds a statement
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA_id}}/messages
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "messageType": "LANDLORD_STATEMENT", "body": "Adding extra context to the claim." }

### 6.2 Admin notes
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA_id}}/messages
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "messageType": "ADMIN_NOTE", "body": "Internal note from admin." }

### 6.3 List all messages
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA_id}}/messages
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}

### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###  7. Penalty-service direct queries
### ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 7.1 List penalties for tenant
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/penalties?tenantId={{tenant_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 7.2 List APPLIED penalties
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/penalties?status=APPLIED
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
